RunInfo: >
  Requires explicit zero-polarization 160 GeV mu+ p and mu+ n samples, with
  POSNLO and NEGNLO generated separately.
NumEvents: 100000
NeedsCrossSection: yes
Beams: [[ANTIMUON, PROTON], [ANTIMUON, NEUTRON]]
Energies: [[160.0, 0.938272], [160.0, 0.939565]]
Description: >
  Fills hadron numerators, matching inclusive-DIS denominators, and
  same-event covariance proxies only in the 311 published sparse (x,y,z)
  cells. Identified pions use truth PID. Unidentified h+/- are stable charged
  hadrons and use the experimental pion-mass assumption in z. The campaign
  postprocessor forms the proton/neutron isoscalar sum before the ratio and
  divides by the z-bin width. Published radiative and diffractive-vector-
  meson correction columns are provenance only and are not applied to Herwig.
